  "description": "ASP.NET Core host check that fails startup when required configuration keys are missing.\n\nCall `IHostBuilder.UseStackContractKeyCheck` with the keys your app must have (for example ConnectionStrings__Default). A hosted service reads IConfiguration at StartAsync; missing or whitespace-only values log ENV_REQUIRED_MISSING and throw InvalidOperationException so the process does not stay up half-configured. Complements Microsoft.Extensions.Options.ValidateOnStart — it checks key presence, not options binding.\n\nThis package does not read Docker Compose or .env files. Use the `stackcontract` global tool in CI for compose/env/appsettings contracts. Internals (StackContract.Core) are bundled; you do not need a separate Core package.\n\nMIT licensed. Not affiliated with Docker, Inc. Repo: https://github.com/munyaimanuwel/stackcontract",
